- **`skills/behavioral-simulation/SKILL.md` + `skills/diverse-thinking/SKILL.md`**
  + **`adapters/agents/src/chat/adapter.ts`** + **`CHAT-ENTRYPOINT.md`**
  + **`scripts/validate-chat-output.mjs`** — novel to AIECP.
  `behavioral-simulation` extends ADR-0010 ("no exception ≠ success")
  from single-scenario verification to multi-scenario end-user-behavior
  simulation; the technique of generating an interaction matrix from
  an `Expected`'s parameter dimensions is original to this project.
  `diverse-thinking` provides seven named cognitive stances
  (first-principles, inverse, analogical, systems, lateral,
  adversarial, constraint-relaxation); the specific list is curated
  from general problem-solving literature (no single upstream
  source), and the procedural "detect stuck → switch style → emit
  Decision → test candidate" pattern is AIECP-original.
  `chat/adapter.ts` + `CHAT-ENTRYPOINT.md` + `validate-chat-output.mjs`
  together implement the text-in/text-out protocol that lets chat LLMs
  without tool use drive the full framework; the protocol design
  (fenced `aiecp:evidence`/`aiecp:memory`/`aiecp:advance`/`aiecp:question`
  code blocks parsed by a validator script) is original to this
  project. No upstream code or prose was adapted or copied.
